From 854431adc02253ae95e710ce9dc336152a66821a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:59:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] metrics: measure admission lock scopes and queue
 backpressure

Measure cs_main wait separately from hold time. The inherited staged
duration fields started before acquiring the lock and therefore included
contention in their purported hold time. Record all admission scopes:
staged input snapshots/commits, asynchronous prepare/verdict handling,
serial peer batches and synchronous RPC snapshots/admission. Also expose
unlocked verification time, queued count/bytes, backpressure events and
disconnect skips. Backpressure events do not discard transactions.

The flood driver normalizes total hold/wait by accepted transactions,
instead of comparing per-batch averages with different batch sizes. It
records the metrics subsystem's dropped-sample counter and omits histogram
timing claims when samples were dropped. Throughput and latency are checked
independently against exact sends, mempool membership and ZMQ notifications.

Validation: assembled Chronik-enabled Release daemon, test and benchmark
targets build; 62 directly related native cases pass. Exact final
functional, TSan and flood evidence is in the delivery README. This does
not claim an extended test suite or patch-progression benchmark sweep.

How to reproduce:
    CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 ninja -C build -j2 bitcoind bitcoin-bench
    contrib/bench/mempool-admission/ab.py \
        --bitcoind new=build/src/bitcoind \
        --config serial=new:-parallelmempool=0 \
        --config par8=new:-parallelmempool=1,-parallelmempoolthreads=8 \
        --fixture FX --workdir AB --peers 8 --rounds 5
The Markdown table reports accepted tx/s, latency p50/p99, CPU, cs_main
hold/wait microseconds per accepted transaction and queue full events.
Raw per-run metrics and accounting checks remain in the JSON results.
